<section class="three-tool-knowledge" id="juz-guide-guide" aria-labelledby="juz-guide-heading">
<h2 id="juz-guide-heading">Quran Juz Finder: all 30 Juz, starting verses and a complete guide</h2>
<p><strong>Short answer:</strong> The Quran is commonly divided into <strong>30 Juz (Ajza or Paras)</strong> for convenient recitation. Juz 1 starts at <strong>1:1</strong>, Juz 2 at <strong>2:142</strong>, and Juz 30 at <strong>78:1 (An-Naba)</strong>. The divisions follow verse references, not a fixed page number across every Mushaf.</p>
